Third-party models and code

This repository contains NO model weights and NO third-party model code.

MolmoAct2 (the vision-language-action model this runtime was built around) is
a work of the Allen Institute for AI, released under the Apache License 2.0:

    Models:  https://huggingface.co/collections/allenai/molmoact2-models
    Code:    https://github.com/allenai/molmoact2
    Paper:   https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02881

Weights are downloaded by the user from the upstream distributor at build
time, under the upstream license, and are never redistributed here. Model
definition code is loaded from the upstream checkpoint via transformers
`trust_remote_code`; this repository carries only a thin compatibility shim
documenting the loading workarounds that checkpoint requires.

Note for anyone deriving artifacts from a checkpoint: a compiled inference
artifact (a TensorRT plan, a CoreML package, an NPU binary) embeds the model
weights and is therefore a derivative work of the checkpoint. Distributing
one distributes the weights. This repository ships build recipes rather than
compiled artifacts, in part for that reason. A prebuilt engine bundle is
published separately as a deliberate, attributed redistribution under the
checkpoint's Apache-2.0 license; its README carries the provenance notes.

Any other policies referenced in documentation are the work of their
respective authors and are likewise not redistributed here.

The files under `examples/bimanual-yam/gello_min/` contain adapted portions of
GELLO from the YAM repository:

    https://github.com/williamtsai726/YAM/tree/main/gello_software

Those portions are licensed under MIT. The required copyright and license
text are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

